  "text": "The upsides first: a little feta can change a whole plate. The salty tang means a small crumble can wake up salads, eggs, wraps, and vegetables. Real Protected Designation of Origin feta has a protected origin story. In the European Union, it has to come from Greece and use sheep's milk, sometimes mixed with goat's milk. The crumble format is genuinely useful. You can spread flavour across a meal without needing a thick slab of cheese.",
